WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.976
Think about a shoe shop. A five-year-old, a teenage footballer and a grandparent all need shoes, but each of them wants something very different.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:20.688
Dividing a market into groups of customers who share similar characteristics is called market segmentation. Each group is a market segment.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:31.396
Choosing which segment to aim your products and promotion at is called targeting. Then the business fits its product, price and promotion to that group.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:47.346
Step one: choose a basis for splitting customers. Common bases are age, income, location, lifestyle and demographics. Demographics means features of the population, such as age, gender and family type.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:59.330
Step two: describe what one segment needs, using facts from the case. Step three: link targeting to a product, price or promotion that fits that need.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:10.187
Step four: end with the result for the business. More sales, more loyal customers, or less money wasted promoting to people who will never buy.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:27.349
Here is a real question from Paper one in November 2023. Explain one benefit to a business of using market segmentation to target its customers. It is worth three marks: one benefit, then two linked steps.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:37.697
Mark one is the benefit. Segmentation lets the business find groups of customers who share similar characteristics, such as the same age or income.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:50.657
Mark two explains why that helps. The business can design a product, set a price and choose promotion that match exactly what that group wants.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:02:01.195
Mark three gives the result. Because the product suits them better, those customers are more likely to buy and to come back, so sales and loyalty rise.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:14.283
Mistake one: confusing segmentation with market research. Research collects information. Segmentation divides customers into groups.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:24.693
Mistake two: naming a basis but not using it. Say how this business would use the basis, and what happens as a result.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:44.819
Now you try. A sports drink company sells one drink to everyone. Identify one basis it could use to segment its market, and explain one benefit of targeting one segment. Pause and decide.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:03:04.117
One good answer uses age. Target teenagers who play sport. Sell smaller bottles at a lower price and promote them on social media. The drink suits them better, so more teenagers buy it and sales rise.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:14.842
That is the pattern for every answer on this type: group the customers, fit the product, price and promotion to them, then show the result. Now try the practice questions.
